{
  "_README": [
    "Custom vocabulary for Gladia speech-to-text. Biases recognition toward",
    "hotel-concierge domain terms so the STT stops mishearing them (the kind",
    "of error seen in production: 'breakfast' -> 'blacksmith', 'amenities' ->",
    "'honesty', 'serveste' -> 'sarbeste').",
    "",
    "HOW TO USE: flatten every array under 'categories' into a single list of",
    "strings and pass it to Gladia's custom_vocabulary parameter (Pipecat's",
    "GladiaSTTService exposes this). Append the proper nouns for the active",
    "hotel from 'hotel_proper_nouns'.",
    "",
    "PER HOTEL: 'hotel_proper_nouns' is keyed by hotel_id. Each hotel's venue",
    "names, dish names and local landmarks should live here. The best source",
    "is the hotel's own RAG knowledge base — those documents already contain",
    "every proper noun (e.g. 'Le Mirador', 'Spa Lumiere'); they can be",
    "auto-extracted. The 'demo' entry below is a worked example.",
    "",
    "LANGUAGE: this file is English ('language': 'en') — the highest-traffic",
    "language and where most errors were observed. Gladia custom vocabulary",
    "can be language-tagged; parallel files (stt_vocabulary.ro.json, etc.)",
    "can be added later. Proper nouns are language-neutral and apply to all.",
    "",
    "LIMIT: if Gladia caps the term count, prioritise 'hotel_proper_nouns'",
    "first, then dining / facilities / concierge_services (the categories",
    "with the most domain-specific, easily-confused words)."
  ],
